# Copy to `.env.development.local` (gitignored) to turn a feature on for your
# own machine.
#
# `.env.development.local`, NOT `.env.local`: Vite loads `.env.local` for
# `vite build` as well, so a value put there is baked into any bundle you build
# on this machine and deployed with it. The `.development.` variant is loaded by
# `vite dev` and ignored by the production build, which is what keeps a local
# opt-in local. The suite pins its own value in `vite.config.ts` and reads
# neither file.
#
# Vite resolves these at BUILD time, so a value set only at run time — a
# Cloudflare Pages runtime variable, a `wrangler secret` — never reaches the
# bundle.

# The Spotify app the workbench signs in to. Unset means the media picker offers
# only YouTube and a local file, which is what the deployed build ships.
#
# It is deliberately not set in production. Spotify's extended quota mode has
# been organizations only since May 2025 (registered business, launched service,
# 250,000 monthly active users), so this app is capped at a hand-added allowlist
# of a few accounts — and a visitor who is not on it is sent to Spotify, signs
# in, and is refused on Spotify's own error page. Offering an answer that cannot
# be carried out is worse than offering one fewer.
#
# Set it there if your Spotify account is on the app's allowlist in the
# developer dashboard. It is not a secret: a client id travels in the authorize
# URL and is inlined in the bundle either way, which is the whole reason PKCE
# needs no client secret.
PUBLIC_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=

# The signed Apple Music developer token. Unlike the Spotify id above, this one
# IS meant to be set in production — Apple has no allowlist and no quota review,
# so any Apple Music subscriber can use it.
#
# Mint it from the Media Services private key, which lives outside this repo:
#
#   bun run token:apple -- --key /path/to/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8
#
# It is not a secret. A developer token is handed to every browser that loads the
# page, which is what makes it safe to inline; the `.p8` that signs it is the
# secret and never leaves the machine that mints it.
#
# It expires within six months — Apple's ceiling. When it does, the picker stops
# offering Apple Music rather than failing under a press, because
# `appleMusicConfigured` reads `exp`. Rotating it is this command, this variable,
# and a redeploy. In production set it as a Cloudflare Pages **build** variable;
# a runtime variable or a `wrangler secret` never reaches the bundle.
PUBLIC_APPLE_MUSIC_TOKEN=

# What the browser tab says while this is a dev server, in place of the draft's
# own name.
#
# The workbench names its tab after the draft, which is named after the song, so
# a dev server and the deployed build open on the same transcription are two
# tabs with the same artist and title in them. This is the word that replaces
# the pair — set it to something more specific if you run two dev servers at
# once.
#
# Unset means the tab is named after the draft, as production is. It is read
# only out of a development build, so a value that ends up in `.env.local` still
# cannot ship.
PUBLIC_DEV_TAB_TITLE=Dev
